{"path":"numeric/complex/Complex_I","title":"_Complex_I","titleHtml":"_Complex_I","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/complex/Complex_I","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"The _Complex_I macro expands to a value of type const float _Complex with the value of the imaginary unit.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex\"><code>&lt;complex.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"co2\">#define _Complex_I /* unspecified */</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The <code>_Complex_I</code> macro expands to a value of type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">float</span> _Complex</span></code> with the value of the imaginary unit.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This macro may be used when <span class=\"t-lc\">I</span> is not available, such as when it has been undefined by the application.\n</p><p>Unlike <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/Imaginary_I\">_Imaginary_I</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/CMPLX\">CMPLX</a></span>, use of this macro to construct a complex number may lose the sign of zero on the imaginary part.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"co2\">#undef I</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#define J _Complex_I // can be used to redefine I</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// can be used to construct a complex number</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> _Complex_I<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"1.0 + 2.0 * _Complex_I =&nbsp;%.1f%+.1fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw753\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw750\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// sign of zero may not be preserved</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> _Complex_I<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"0.0 + -0.0 * _Complex_I =&nbsp;%.1f%+.1fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw753\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw750\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>1.0 + 2.0 * _Complex_I = 1.0+2.0i\n0.0 + -0.0 * _Complex_I = 0.0+0.0i</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-23\">\n<ul><li> C23 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.1/4 _Complex_I (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.1/4 _Complex_I (p: 136)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.1/4 _Complex_I (p: 188)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.1/2 _Complex_I (p: 170)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/Imaginary_I\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>_Imaginary_I</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   the imaginary unit constant i <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(macro constant)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/I\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>I</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   the complex or imaginary unit constant i <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(macro constant)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"Complex number arithmetic"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"_Complex_I","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. The _Complex_I macro expands to a value of type const float _Complex with the value of the imaginary unit."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This macro may be used when I is not available, such as when it has been undefined by the application."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"_Imaginary_I","note":"the imaginary unit constant i"},{"label":"I","note":"the complex or imaginary unit constant i"}]}]},"standards":["C99"],"wordCount":217,"codeBlockCount":2}
